  "limits": [
    "Siderite and altered pyrrhotite are impure natural feeds, not the humboldtine owner or pure reagents. No inherited criticality.",
    "2021 day-three pyrrhotite morphology/EDX is not day-three PXRD; confirmed phase later. Quantitative dissolution rates/oxalate/redox and source-specific iron balance absent.",
    "2021 medium includes FeSO4, no no-rock/killed/filtrate or pH-matched controls; controls have qualitative absence of iron-oxalate crystals, not zero-yield measurement.",
    "2021 pH is initially 5.5 in Methods, later 3.5 +/- 0.5 called initial in Results; no silent reconciliation.",
    "2023 Table 4 differentiates method-specific assignments and missing products; C. puteana siderite is microscopy-only, A. xantha pyrrhotite has only whewellite; S. lacrymans iron arms have dashes, not numeric zero.",
    "2023 Figure 7b labels whewellite with humboldtine on A. xantha/siderite; Table 4 lists only humboldtine.",
    "2023 uninoculated controls described but no separate iron-arm outcome data/phase plots; liquid GPL recipe not separately tabulated; agar formulation includes iron.",
    "A.niger comparison in 2023 relies on earlier publications, not a same-medium iron-feed comparator. No supported superiority/rate/yield/industrial claim.",
    "GenBank KY433983.1 and official taxonomy XML ScientificName use Amyloporia xantha; browser heading agrees but its current-name field says Antrodia xantha. Both names and shared ID retained.",
    "Field calcium oxalates in 2023 and field goethite in 2021 are not environmental humboldtine proof.",
    "Neither paper declares SI in full PDF/XML; no raw replicate diffraction series/solution concentrations are deposited in the inspected artifacts."
  ],
